### =====================================================================
### TRIPS
###
### Run these top to bottom the first time. Requests 1-2 get you a token,
### 3-8 are the happy path, 9-13 are the permission checks.
### =====================================================================

@supabaseUrl = https://usivgxovisdhfqneffto.supabase.co
@publishableKey = sb_publishable_7lOB5WANGC3tMzzxh7Loqg_sNqEOuEE
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### 1. Sign in as the primary test user
# @name signin
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123"
}

###
@token = {{signin.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. Create a second account, used for the permission checks below.
### Only needs to succeed once; a duplicate signup error on later runs is fine.
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/signup
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "outsider@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123"
}

### 3. Sign in as the outsider
# @name outsiderSignin
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password
apikey: {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "outsider@example.com",
  "password": "testpassword123"
}

###
@outsiderToken = {{outsiderSignin.response.body.access_token}}


### =====================================================================
### HAPPY PATH
### =====================================================================

### 4. Create a trip
### EXPECT 201. Copy the returned id into @tripId below.
### Then check db:studio: trip_members must have an OWNER row for you.
# @name createTrip
POST {{baseUrl}}/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Smoke Test Trip",
  "description": "Created from trip.http",
  "destination": "Orlando, FL",
  "startDate": "2027-06-12",
  "endDate": "2027-06-17"
}

###
@tripId = {{createTrip.response.body.trip.id}}

### 5. List my trips
### EXPECT 200. The new trip appears with memberCount 1, yourRole OWNER,
### status UPCOMING.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Trip detail
### EXPECT 200 with the full member roster and yourRole OWNER.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Update the trip
### EXPECT 200 with the new name.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Smoke Test Trip (renamed)"
}

### 8. Update just the end date
### EXPECT 200. Checks the merged-date rule: the schema cannot compare one
### date on its own, so the controller re-checks against the stored start date.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endDate": "2027-06-20"
}


### =====================================================================
### VALIDATION
### =====================================================================

### 9. End date before start date
### EXPECT 422, with details pointing at endDate.
POST {{baseUrl}}/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Backwards Trip",
  "destination": "Nowhere",
  "startDate": "2027-06-17",
  "endDate": "2027-06-12"
}

### 10. Empty name
### EXPECT 422.
POST {{baseUrl}}/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "destination": "Orlando, FL",
  "startDate": "2027-06-12",
  "endDate": "2027-06-17"
}

### 11. Empty PATCH body
### EXPECT 422 - a no-op update is almost always a client bug.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### =====================================================================
### PERMISSIONS
### =====================================================================

### 12. Non-member reads the trip
### EXPECT 404, NOT 403. A 403 would confirm the trip exists and let someone
### walk ids to discover real ones.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{outsiderToken}}

### 13. Non-member updates the trip
### EXPECT 404.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{outsiderToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hijacked"
}

### 14. Non-member lists trips
### EXPECT 200 with an empty array - they have no trips, and they learn
### nothing about anyone else's.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{outsiderToken}}

### 15. No token at all
### EXPECT 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips

### 16. Unknown trip id
### EXPECT 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips/00000000-0000-7000-8000-ffffffffffff
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =====================================================================
### SEARCH, FILTER, SORT
###
### These read best against the seeded demo trip plus the smoke test trip,
### so run `npm run db:seed` first and set DEV_USER_ID in prisma/seed.ts to
### your own Supabase user id.
### =====================================================================

### 19. Search by name
### EXPECT 200, only trips whose name or destination contains "orlando".
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?search=orlando
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. Search is case-insensitive
### EXPECT 200, the same results as #19.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?search=ORLANDO
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 21. Search matches destination, not just name
### EXPECT 200, the Orlando trip - matched on destination "Orlando, FL".
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?search=FL
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22. Empty search returns everything
### EXPECT 200, all your trips. `?search=` is what a cleared input sends, and
### it must not be treated as a search for the empty string.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?search=
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23. Filter by status
### EXPECT 200, only trips whose start date is in the future. Every returned
### trip must also have "status": "UPCOMING" in its body - that agreement
### between the filter and the derived field is the thing to check.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?status=UPCOMING
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Filter by role
### EXPECT 200, only trips where you are the OWNER.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?role=OWNER
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Sort by name, descending
### EXPECT 200, reverse alphabetical.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?sort=name&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. Everything at once
### EXPECT 200. Filters compose with AND, so this is
### (my trips) AND (owner) AND (upcoming) AND (name or destination matches).
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?search=trip&status=UPCOMING&role=OWNER&sort=startDate&order=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 27. Unknown sort field
### EXPECT 422. The enum is what stops a caller ordering by an arbitrary column.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?sort=description
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28. Unknown status
### EXPECT 422.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips?status=CANCELLED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### =====================================================================
### MEMBER vs OWNER
###
### SETUP: you need a trip where you are a MEMBER rather than the OWNER.
### Fastest way, no code needed:
###   1. npm run db:studio
###   2. open trip_members, find your row on the seeded Orlando trip
###   3. change role from OWNER to MEMBER, save
###   4. run #29 and #30
###   5. change it back to OWNER
###
### Paste that trip's id here:
### =====================================================================

@memberTripId = 01a12cbc-5808-761e-ac70-2f9a0084a06a

### 29. MEMBER tries to update
### EXPECT 403 FORBIDDEN - not 404. They already know the trip exists because
### they are in it, so hiding it would be pointless and confusing.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{memberTripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A member should not be able to do this"
}

### 30. MEMBER tries to delete
### EXPECT 403.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{memberTripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 31. MEMBER can still read
### EXPECT 200 with "yourRole": "MEMBER".
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{memberTripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =====================================================================
### CLEANUP
### =====================================================================

### 32. Delete the smoke test trip
### EXPECT 204 with an empty body. Check db:studio - the trip_members row
### is gone too, via cascade.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 33. Confirm it is gone
### EXPECT 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
